# Student Result Management System

This is my first beginner-level Python mini project.

## 📌 Description

This is a simple console-based Python program that takes a student's name
and marks as input and determines the result based on the marks entered.

The program classifies the result into:
- Distinction
- First Class
- Pass
- Fail

It uses conditional statements to evaluate the marks and display the appropriate result.


## 🚀 Features

- Accept student name as input
- Accept student marks as input
- Classify result based on marks
- Display formatted result output
- Uses loop structure for repeated execution

## 🧠 Concepts Used

- Variables
- Input / Output
- Type casting (float)
- if-elif-else conditions
- while loop
- Basic logical comparison

## 🎯 Purpose

This project was created as my first step in learning Python.
It helped me understand how conditional statements and loops work in real programs.

